+ *
+ * poly_nir_lower_gs() (src/poly/nir/poly_nir_lower_gs.c, shared with Honeykrisp)
+ * rewrites the API geometry shader into up to four programs:
+ *
+ *   MAIN  compute, one thread per input primitive. Runs the GS body and, for a
+ *         dynamic output topology, writes the vertex indices it produced into an
+ *         index buffer allocated out of the device heap.
+ *   COUNT compute, same shape as MAIN but stripped to just the output counts.
+ *         Only needed when the vertex count is not a compile-time constant AND
+ *         someone reads those counts, which today means transform feedback.
+ *   PRE   a 1x1x1 kernel that patches up transform feedback offsets and the
+ *         GS/clipper pipeline-statistics counters.
+ *   RAST  a *vertex* shader that re-runs the GS body and selects the one output
+ *         vertex the hardware asked for. This becomes the Metal render
